hello everyone and welcome to math  simplified i'm dr omar malik and welcome  to our new video series known as  superfood sundays  where every sunday we will discuss one  superfood that has immense health  benefits and also how you can  incorporate that food into your daily  diet  according to many dietitians a superfood  offers high levels of desirable  nutrients linked to promoting personal  health and wellness or preventing  disease and sickness  such desirable nutrients include  antioxidants anti-inflammatory agents  and other vitamin and trace element rich  foods  so let's begin and to start off the  series the superfood that we will  discuss this sunday is turmeric  turmeric scientifically known as curcuma  longa is a bright yellow spice used  throughout asia for centuries  grown for its root turmeric has an  ancient history of uses in cooking  fabric dyeing cosmetics and especially  as a traditional medicine in china and  india  its use in conditions such as rheumatism  severe pain fatigue and breathing  problems has been well documented for  over 4 000 years  scientists have identified a key  ingredient of turmeric that quite  literally gives turmeric its superfood  properties this key ingredient is known  as curcumin  curcumin is a pigment found in turmeric  that not only gives it its  characteristic bright yellow hue but  also has a range of health benefits  these include antibacterial  antimicrobial anti-inflammatory and  antioxidant effects  because of these wide ranging functions  turmeric has been studied in relation to  arthritis eye conditions cancer heart  diseases alzheimer's disease and much  more  so let's talk about some of these top  scientifically proven health benefits of  turmeric  number one curcumin is a natural  anti-inflammatory compound  inflammation is incredibly important for  our body it helps to fight bacteria and  viruses and also has a role in repairing  the damage done in your body by free  radicals it's a body's way of protecting  itself  although short-term inflammation is  beneficial it can be a concern if it  becomes long-term or chronic and attacks  your body's own tissues chronic low  level inflammation plays a key role in  the development of many diseases  including heart diseases cancer  metabolic syndrome alzheimer's disease  and various degenerative conditions  that's why anything that can help to  fight chronic inflammation is important  in the prevention and treatment of these  conditions  the curcumin in turmeric has proven  strong anti-inflammatory properties that  reduce the damage done by chronic  inflammation in the body  studies have shown positive effects of  curcumin on people suffering from  conditions such as rheumatoid arthritis  inflammatory bowel disease and many  others  this anti-inflammatory ability of  turmeric reduces the worsening of  pre-existing joint problems as well as  development of new ones in the people  with arthritis  in addition turmeric also has pain  relieving properties  the spice is reputed to relieve  arthritis pain as well  dietitians suggest taking turmeric  capsules of 400 to 600 milligrams up to  three times per day number two  turmeric is a powerful antioxidant  curcumin has potent antioxidant  properties  now to completely explain what oxidative  damage is what free radicals are and how  antioxidant work  we need a whole another video but to cut  it short just remember oxidative damage  is believed to be one of the main  mechanisms behind aging and the  development of many chronic diseases the  main reasons antioxidants are so  beneficial is that they protect your  body from this oxidative damage and the  development of many diseases like  cataracts glaucoma and macular  degeneration in the eyes  number three curcumin can boost brain  health  before scientists had a better  understanding of neurons it was believed  that they were not able to divide and  multiply after early childhood but  studies have shown this isn't true  neurons are capable of forming new  connections and in certain areas the  brain they can multiply and increase in  number also  one of the main drivers of this process  is brain derived neurotrophic factor  also known as bdnf  this protein is responsible for  promoting the life of neurons and also  plays a role in memory and learning  many common brain disorders have been  linked to the decreased levels of pdnf  protein including depression and  alzheimer's disease  interestingly animal studies have shown  that curcumin may increase the levels of  bdnf in the brain  by doing this it may be effective in the  delaying or even reversing many brain  diseases and age related decrease in  brain function  also there is growing evidence that  curcumin can cross the blood-brain  barrier and may help to protect against  alzheimer's disease  it works to reduce inflammation as well  as the buildup of protein plaques in the  brain that are characteristic of  alzheimer's disease sufferers still  since these studies were performed in  animals it's hard to say what the  results mean for humans and more studies  are needed to confirm this  number four curcumin may lower your risk  of heart diseases  heart disease is the number one cause of  death in the world  researchers have studied it for many  decades and learned a lot about why it  happens  unsurprisingly heart disease is  incredibly complicated and various  things contribute to it including  oxidative stress by free radicals  curcumin may help to reverse many steps  in the heart disease process  perhaps the main benefit of curcumin  when it comes to heart disease is  improving the function of endothelium  which is the inner lining of your blood  vessels  when endothelium gets affected it is  unable to regulate blood pressure blood  clotting and various other factors and  this dysfunction is a major driver of  heart diseases  several studies suggest that curcumin  can lead to improvement in the health of  endothelium  one study found that regular consumption  of turmeric is as effective as exercise  in post-menopausal females  in addition curcumin can help to reduce  inflammation and oxidative damage which  can play a key role in the development  of heart diseases  in one study of 121 people undergoing  coronary artery bypass surgery  researchers assigned them into two  groups  one group received a placebo and the  other group received 4 grams of curcumin  per day for a few days before and after  the surgery they found that the group  who took curcumin had a 65 decreased  risk of experiencing a heart attack in  the hospital  indicating that turmeric definitively  reduces their heart related issues  number five turmeric may help to prevent  cancer also  cancer is a disease characterized by  uncontrolled cell growth there are many  different forms of cancer that appear to  be affected by curcumin supplements  curcumin has been studied as a  beneficial herb in the cancer treatment  and has been found to affect cancer  growth and development  studies have shown that it has various  ways that it can control cancer such as  it contributes to the death of cancerous  cells it reduces angiogenesis which  means it prevents growth of new blood  vessels in the tumor  and it reduces metastasis also that is  the spread of cancer  whether high dose curcumin preferably  with an absorption enhancer can help to  treat cancer has yet to be studied  properly  however there is evidence that it may  prevent cancer from occurring in the  first place  especially cancers of the digestive  system like colorectal cancer this was  studied by researchers in a month-long  study in 44 men these men had lesions in  the colon that sometimes turned  cancerous the researchers found that 4  grams of curcumin per day reduces the  number of lesions by 40  so the bottom line is that turmeric and  especially its most active compound  curcumin have many scientifically proven  health benefits such as the potential to  improve heart health prevention against  alzheimer's and cancer  relieving joint pain in arthritis and  much more it's a potent  anti-inflammatory and antioxidant agent  while these benefits are possible they  are limited at this time because of the  curcumin scars bioavailability  the current scientific literature  regarding definitive benefit of turmeric  is still in its early development  so while scientists explore the benefits  of turmeric in their own way you can  introduce turmeric in one form or other  in your diet and start experiencing the  benefits yourself  you have the advice of billions of  people who have used turmeric for  innumerable purposes over the last four  thousand years well thank you for  watching this video don't forget to like  share and subscribe become a member of  our channel on youtube or support us via  patreon we at med simplified appreciate  your feedback and look forward to your  continued support as always take care  and i'll see you in the next video
 

